# Project-specific Data Directories (from your config.py)
# These directories will contain generated files or input media
# and should generally not be versioned.
# If you have small sample files for testing within these directories
# that you DO want to version, you can add exceptions like:
# !audio/sample_test.mp3
audio/
transcriptions/
backup/
embeddings/

# Log files and directories
logs/
*.log
# If your LOG_FILE is directly in the root or another non-ignored dir:
# transcription_errors.log

# Configuration files that might contain sensitive data or local paths
# If you have local customizations to config.py, create config.local.py
# and add sensitive settings there instead
config.local.py

# IDE and Editor specific files
.vscode/
.idea/
*.sublime-project
*.sublime-workspace
*.komodoproject/
.project
.settings/
*.tmproj

# Spell checker configuration files
.cspell.json
.cspell-dict.txt

# Documentation files
CHANGELOG.md

# Operating System specific files
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
ehthumbs.db
Desktop.ini
NTUSER.DAT*

# Temporary files
*.tmp
*.swp
*.swo

# Lock files (if any generated by other tools, your script handles its own .lock)
# Example: package-lock.json if you were using npm for something, or poetry.lock if it's in a place you don't want
# For this project, the .lock files generated by the script are within the data directories
# which are already ignored, so no specific rule needed here for them.

# Jupyter Notebook checkpoints
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# Security - if you ever use mkcert for local HTTPS
*.pem
*.key
*.csr